    "solution": "**Passo 1: Potenze dissipate sui resistori**\\n$$P_{R1} = \frac{E^2}{R_1} = \frac{24^2}{6} = \frac{576}{6} = 96\text{ W}$$\\n$$P_{R2} = \frac{E^2}{R_2} = \frac{24^2}{12} = \frac{576}{12} = 48\text{ W}$$\\n$$P_{diss,tot} = 96 + 48 = 144\text{ W}$$\\n\\n**Passo 2: Potenza erogata da E**\\n$$I_E = I_1 + I_2 = \frac{24}{6} + \frac{24}{12} = 4 + 2 = 6\text{ A}$$\\n$$P_{erog} = E \\cdot I_E = 24 \\cdot 6 = 144\text{ W}$$\\n\\nPer il Teorema di Tellegen: $\\sum_{k} v_k i_k = 0 \\implies P_{erog} = P_{diss}$.",
